From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:19:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] PCI: apple: let devices below a kernel-trained port
 leave D0 over s2idle

The adopted-link s2idle check walked the whole bus and refused to suspend
when any device had left D0. With a kernel-trained second port (the SD
reader on the K116s) the PCI core puts that root port into D3hot, and
suspend failed with -EBUSY. Below a port Linux trained itself, only the
devices that asked to stay awake need to remain in D0; the PCI core
restores the rest. Below a port the boot loader trained, such as the
N1's, every device must still be in D0, so the J716c and the K114c, whose
only port is adopted, are checked as before.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
[thomas: skip only devices below a port Linux trained (port->pwren), so
 adopted ports keep requiring D0 for every device]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Glanzmann <thomas@glanzmann.de>

(cherry picked from commit 70bf8ed1867b2b322c89f3a74e4f51a6547dc1fe)
[k114s: from aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1647 (open), unchanged]
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index 64cf71162..1b87ff0fa 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -5711,6 +5711,22 @@ static void apple_pcie_stop_for_sleep(struct device *dev)
 
 static void apple_pcie_neo_save_functions(struct apple_pcie *pcie);
 
+/* Whether Linux trained the port above pdev itself (cold train), rather than adopting it */
+static bool apple_pcie_below_kernel_trained_port(struct pci_dev *pdev)
+{
+	struct pci_config_window *cfg = pdev->sysdata;
+	struct apple_pcie *pcie = apple_pcie_lookup(cfg->parent);
+	struct pci_dev *rp = pcie_find_root_port(pdev);
+	struct apple_pcie_port *port;
+
+	if (!rp)
+		return false;
+	list_for_each_entry(port, &pcie->ports, entry)
+		if (port->idx == PCI_SLOT(rp->devfn))
+			return !!port->pwren;
+	return false;
+}
+
 /*
  * The J716c radio drivers save PCI state without entering D3. The PCI core
  * keeps the root port in D0 as well. Its host and DART have no switchable
@@ -5725,6 +5741,16 @@ static int apple_pcie_check_d0(struct pci_dev *pdev, void *data)
 	int *error = data;
 	u16 value;
 
+	/*
+	 * Below a port the boot loader trained (the N1's), every device stays
+	 * in D0. Below a port Linux trained itself (the K116s SD reader's), the
+	 * PCI core restores what it suspends to D3hot, so only the devices that
+	 * asked to stay awake need to remain in D0.
+	 */
+	if (!device_awake_path(&pdev->dev) &&
+	    apple_pcie_below_kernel_trained_port(pdev))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (pci_read_config_word(pdev, PCI_VENDOR_ID, &value) ||
 	    value != pdev->vendor) {
 		*error = -ENODEV;
